nodecode-gurusup-brain is a rewrite of gurusup's gurusup/gurusup-brain-plugin:

  https://github.com/gurusup/gurusup-brain-plugin
  commit 4709ca345cb55a1fab809b6b53523c5c0600be6e

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 GuruSup (LICENSE)

The original is a package of manifests and one skill: `plugin.json`, `mcp.json`
and `.mcp.json` and `server.json` and the `.claude-plugin/` entries declare one
remote MCP server (`https://mcp.brain.gurusup.com/mcp`), and
`skills/using-brain/SKILL.md` tells the model to call that server's `init` tool
first, to base answers about the company on the evidence it returns, and to say
so when there is too little. What was rewritten is the transport and the skill:
`wire.lisp` speaks MCP's streamable HTTP to the same endpoint over a bearer
token from the config section, `tools.lisp` gives the model one tool to list
what the account may call, one to fetch the init contract and one to call any
of them by name, and `cell.lisp` carries the skill's rules as the
`(help :gurusup-brain)` topic plus a `/gurusup-brain` command. Left out: the
OAuth browser sign-in (a cell takes the token the sign-in issues), the manifest
and marketplace files that only describe the package to other clients, and any
assumption about the server's own tool names, which are read from its
`tools/list`. No code from the original runs here; it ships none.
